# GitHub / Git credentials template
# ---------------------------------
# Copy this file to  config/git_credentials.env  (untracked, private) and fill
# it in. NEVER commit the real file, never paste the token into a chat/screen.

# How to create a token (GitHub):
#   1. GitHub -> Settings -> Developer settings -> Personal access tokens.
#   2. "Tokens (classic)" -> Generate new token.
#   3. Scope: only the minimum you need, e.g. `repo` for private repos pushes.
#   4. Copy it immediately - it is shown only once. Keep it secret.
#   5. When done, revoke/rotate it under the same page.

# Who is pushing (your GitHub username)
GITHUB_USER=

# A Personal Access Token (startswith ghp_ for classic, ghp_ / ghu_ / ghs_ ...
# and "fine-grained" tokens look different). Treat it like a password.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Optional: the HTTPS remote URL WITHOUT the token, e.g.
# https://github.com/<your-user>/<your-repo>.git
# The token is inserted at push time by the helper, never stored in the URL.
GIT_REMOTE_URL=

# --- Safety rules -----------------------------------------------------------
# * The real file is listed in config/.gitignore and must never be committed.
# * The notebook helper reads it, but never prints the token.
# * Prefer a short-lived, minimal-scope token. Audit it from time to time.
# * If a token ever leaks, revoke it immediately on GitHub.